{"ts":"2026-07-28T02:54:39.018Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"f76875cfa69f9541795a0949","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-cb8qq2"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-782: guide-shell special-cases one multi-word command name and duplicates its status derivation, and calendar's throw-only validation call is unexplained, inside package-managed built-ins consumers cannot patch"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-782.\n\nThree runtime-maintainability gaps in the managed calendar and guide-shell built-ins, reported against published 2026.7.27. They are individually small, but the files are package-managed, so a downstream repository cannot sustainably patch them and each one is a latent behaviour-drift site.\n\nReported findings:\n\n- guide-shell maps update-many to update_many with a one-command special case. Registry lookup should normalize every multi-word command name consistently, for example by translating hyphens and whitespace to underscores, before falling back to an empty definition. As written, the second multi-word command to arrive silently resolves to an empty definition instead of its registry entry, and the failure is a missing capability rather than an error.\n- guide-shell derives the filtered, locale-sorted status-ID list twice, once during initialization and once during completion-status execution. Two copies of one derivation is the standard precondition for the two diverging under later edits.\n- calendar calls resolveCalendarOutputFormat standalone purely so that it throws on an invalid format before runCalendar, but nothing records that the call is throw-only, so it reads as a dead result and invites removal.\n\nThe unifying point is that a special case, a duplicated derivation and an unexplained throw-only call are each a place where the next edit can change behaviour without any gate noticing, inside artifacts that consumers cannot repair."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Chore"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["extensions","maintainability"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-28T02:54:39.018Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-28T02:54:39.018Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"guide-shell normalizes every multi-word command name through one generic rule rather than a per-command special case, covered by a test that adds a second multi-word command; The filtered locale-sorted status-ID derivation exists once in guide-shell and both call sites use it; The throw-only purpose of the standalone resolveCalendarOutputFormat call in calendar is recorded so the call cannot be removed as dead code; GH-782 is closed with evidence that the normalizer handles a command name it was not written for"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":92},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-92if","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-28T02:54:39.018Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-vnk7ob","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-28T02:54:39.018Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"00327882f46e30e970f4604b2f49e4f9e9b09517a50b251239c9e173c9080b6f","message":""}
